Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:45:38 +0100
Subject: NIFI-16547 Add connect timeout to cluster protocol sockets

SocketUtils.createSocket connected without a timeout, so connecting to a peer that silently drops packets (like the old IP of a restarted Kubernetes pod) hung until the OS gave up after roughly two minutes. That stalled heartbeats and the heartbeat monitor on the coordinator.

Sockets are now created unconnected and then connected using nifi.cluster.node connection.timeout. A connect timeout when notifying a node about its own status change is no longer retried, same as a refused connection already wasn't. The hostname still gets resolved on every attempt, exactly like before, so we don't hang on to stale IPs.
